# Reviewed required-suite exceptions for GCC 16.2.0 built in the LFS chroot and
# tested as the unprivileged tester account. Format and review rules: README.md
# in this directory.
#
# Basis: The LFS 13.1-systemd GCC page lists the tests known to fail for this
#   version (in gcc.target/i386: auto-init-padding-9.c, builtin-memmove-*.c,
#   mem{cpy,set}-pr120683-*.c, pr111657-1.c, pr115102.c, pr116896.c,
#   pr120881-2a.c and pr122343-4a.c; in g++.target/i386:
#   memset-pr108585-1{a,b}.C, mv{,c}-symbols*.C, pr112824-2.C and
#   pr116896-1.C; and gcc.dg/ipa/pr122458.c, gcc.dg/lto/toplevel-*-asm-* and
#   gcc.dg/plugin/crash-test-nested-*.c), says most of them come from test
#   authors not anticipating --enable-default-ssp or --enable-default-pie, and
#   tells builders to compare with its reference results.
#   https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/view/13.1-systemd/chapter08/gcc.html
#   68 of the lines below match those names. The other six
#   (gcc.target/i386 memset-pr70308-1a.c, memset-pr70308-1b.c, pr125355.c,
#   pr125355-2.c and two results of xchg-4.c) are not named on the page. All
#   74 lines, those six included, occur byte for byte in the LFS editors'
#   reference test log for this book version and compiler:
#   https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/build-logs/13.1/i7-14700K/test-logs/830-gcc-16.2.0
#   (177526 bytes, sha256 271d2913bcfcbb3c24c2c11a72ac8a7dfb74bb04ec9b53eec854f9814aa4d855,
#   fetched 2026-11-05). That log's only further result,
#   "FAIL: gcc.target/i386/shift-gf2p8affine-2.c execution test", is the one
#   the page ties to processors without AVX512; it passed here and is not
#   listed. The cause of the six unnamed results was not traced separately.
# Observed: rehearsal attempt 03 on 2026-11-05, an isolated continuation of
#   failed core run 001 with this page's recipe unchanged, four test jobs:
#   511259 expected passes in six summaries (g++ 267590, gcc 218851,
#   libstdc++ 18597, libgomp 6123, libatomic 54, libitm 44), 72 unexpected
#   failures (gcc 39, g++ 33) and 2 unexpected successes (gcc), no UNRESOLVED
#   or ERROR. The reference log has the same counts except gcc 218831 passes
#   and 40 failures.
@min-pass 511000
